{
  "slug": "one-pager-writing",
  "concept": "One-Pager Writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "One-pagers are the highest-impact document format in business: a single page that earns a meeting, secures a budget, aligns a partner, or briefs an exec in under three minutes.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "One-pagers are the highest-impact document format in business: a single page that earns a meeting, secures a budget, aligns a partner, or briefs an exec in under three minutes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. The no-second-page discipline",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A one-pager fits on one page. The moment you flow to page 2, the document is now a half-finished two-pager. Everything else in this skill exists to enforce this rule.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#1-the-no-second-page-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Cut by 30-50% from your first draft. Always.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#1-the-no-second-page-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Drop full sentences for fragments where fragments work.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#1-the-no-second-page-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Move evidence to an appendix link, not a footer.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#1-the-no-second-page-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "If three things won't fit, you have three things - not one.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#1-the-no-second-page-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Above-the-fold visual hierarchy",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The reader scans before they read. What lives above the fold:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#2-above-the-fold-visual-hierarchy",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Headline - the one-line value prop, written in the reader's language.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#2-above-the-fold-visual-hierarchy",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Subhead or value-prop sentence - what changes for the reader if they say yes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#2-above-the-fold-visual-hierarchy",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "The \"if you only read one line\" sentence - bolded, set off visually.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#2-above-the-fold-visual-hierarchy",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "A visual anchor - chart, screenshot, diagram, photo, or large pull-quote.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#2-above-the-fold-visual-hierarchy",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. The \"if you only read one line\" pattern",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every one-pager has one sentence the reader must take away. Find it. Bold it. Place it above the fold. Repeat it in different words at the end.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#3-the-if-you-only-read-one-line-pattern",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. The Amazon 1-pager and the PR/FAQ lineage",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The Amazon 1-pager / PR-style opener:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#5-the-amazon-1-pager-and-the-prfaq-lineage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Heading: the product or initiative name.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#5-the-amazon-1-pager-and-the-prfaq-lineage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Subheading: who it's for, in their language.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#5-the-amazon-1-pager-and-the-prfaq-lineage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Summary paragraph (3-4 sentences): what it does, who benefits, why now.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#5-the-amazon-1-pager-and-the-prfaq-lineage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Problem paragraph: the customer's status quo.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#5-the-amazon-1-pager-and-the-prfaq-lineage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Solution paragraph: how this changes the status quo.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#5-the-amazon-1-pager-and-the-prfaq-lineage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Quote (optional): an executive or customer making the value claim concrete.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#5-the-amazon-1-pager-and-the-prfaq-lineage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Call to action: what the reader does next.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#5-the-amazon-1-pager-and-the-prfaq-lineage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Two non-negotiables: written as full sentences; written as if the product already launched.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#5-the-amazon-1-pager-and-the-prfaq-lineage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Bullets vs paragraphs",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use paragraphs when: The reader needs to see how ideas connect; describing a customer's strategic status quo; Amazon 1-pager opener.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#6-bullets-vs-paragraphs",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Use bullets when: Listing 3-7 parallel items; scannable facts; the reader is an exec who triages.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#6-bullets-vs-paragraphs",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Heuristic: paragraphs for the upper half (the narrative), bullets for the lower half (the facts and the ask).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#6-bullets-vs-paragraphs",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Section budget for a single page",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A single page gives you roughly 550-650 words of usable real estate:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#7-section-budget-for-a-single-page",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Headline + value prop: 20-30 words",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#7-section-budget-for-a-single-page",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Above-the-fold callout: 15-25 words",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#7-section-budget-for-a-single-page",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Body - problem / context: 80-120 words",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#7-section-budget-for-a-single-page",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Body - solution / approach: 100-150 words",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#7-section-budget-for-a-single-page",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Body - outcomes / proof: 80-120 words",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#7-section-budget-for-a-single-page",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "The ask: 30-50 words",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#7-section-budget-for-a-single-page",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9. The five canonical species",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Account brief - for an internal audience to brief before a customer meeting.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#9-the-five-canonical-species",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Project pitch - to get funding or headcount.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#9-the-five-canonical-species",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Product one-pager - for stakeholders evaluating a product.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#9-the-five-canonical-species",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Sales-enablement one-pager - for sellers to use in front of buyers.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#9-the-five-canonical-species",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Amazon 1-pager / PR-FAQ opener - for internal alignment on a new product.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#9-the-five-canonical-species",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "10. The ask, the owner, the next step",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every one-pager ends with:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#10-the-ask-the-owner-the-next-step",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The ask - what specific thing do you need from the reader. A verb with an object.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#10-the-ask-the-owner-the-next-step",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "The owner - who runs this, with name, role, contact.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#10-the-ask-the-owner-the-next-step",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "The next step - when, where, what format.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#10-the-ask-the-owner-the-next-step",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "These three sentences are the entire reason the one-pager exists. Never cut these.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#10-the-ask-the-owner-the-next-step",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The 1.5-pager - runs onto a second page by half a paragraph.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The mystery headline - \"Project Phoenix: A New Approach.\" No value visible.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The ask buried at line 47 - the ask should be visible above the fold.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The \"alignment\" ask - \"We're seeking alignment on...\" No verb, no object.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The missing owner line - the page is anonymous.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The four-CTA ending - list more than two CTAs and readers pick zero.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/one-pager-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
